{"id": "stlurban", "name": "Urban St. Louis", "short": "Urban St. Louis", "place": "St. Louis, Missouri, USA", "lat": 38.63, "lon": -90.25, "side": "l", "blurb": "Oaks, squirrels, city coyotes and falcons in Forest Park and the neighborhoods.", "tip": {"id": "coyote", "title": "Remove the city coyote", "text": "Coyotes are the top predator on the ground in St. Louis parks. Set Coyote to -100% and watch rabbits, deer and raccoons."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Forest Park (St. Louis)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest_Park_(St._Louis)"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Urban coyote", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_coyote"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Peregrine falcon", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peregrine_falcon"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Cooper's hawk", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cooper%27s_hawk"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Chimney swift", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chimney_swift"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Raccoon", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raccoon"}], "notes": "Feeding links were checked against the sources listed where they state them. Where the sources are silent, links come from general ecological knowledge and are illustrative. Feeding links that match a GloBI (Global Biotic Interactions) record are marked in the node details, with a link to the records. A few links were added from GloBI records.", "imgwiki": "Forest Park (St. Louis)", "icon": "rsquirrel", "tier": "overview", "cont": "North America", "country": "United States of America", "states": ["Missouri", "Illinois"], "nodes": [{"id": "oak", "sp": "quercus spp.", "xh": 0.1, "name": "Street & park oaks", "wiki": "Quercus", "desc": "Large shade trees of St. Louis parks and streets. Their acorns feed squirrels and deer, and their leaves host many caterpillars."}, {"id": "maple", "sp": "acer spp.", "xh": 0.24}, {"id": "lawn", "sp": "poaceae", "xh": 0.45, "name": "Lawns & park turf", "wiki": "Lawn", "desc": "Mown grass that covers much of the city's parks 